Task 1: Create Machine Credentials for Secure Login
Machine credentials allow Ansible Automation Platform to authenticate and connect to managed hosts securely. We'll create SSH-based credentials for system access.

Subtask 1.1: Generate SSH Key Pair
First, we'll create an SSH key pair that will be used for machine authentication.

Access your control node terminal and generate a new SSH key pair:
ssh-keygen -t rsa -b 4096 -C "ansible-automation" -f ~/.ssh/ansible_key
Press Enter when prompted for a passphrase to create a key without a passphrase (for automation purposes):
# Output should show:
# Generating public/private rsa key pair.
# Enter passphrase (empty for no passphrase): [Press Enter]
# Enter same passphrase again: [Press Enter]
# Your identification has been saved in /home/student/.ssh/ansible_key
# Your public key has been saved in /home/student/.ssh/ansible_key.pub
Verify the key creation:
ls -la ~/.ssh/ansible_key*
Display the private key content (we'll need this for credential creation):
cat ~/.ssh/ansible_key
Copy the private key content to your clipboard or notepad for later use.
Subtask 1.2: Distribute Public Key to Target Hosts
Copy the public key to target hosts (replace target-host-ip with actual IP addresses):
ssh-copy-id -i ~/.ssh/ansible_key.pub student@target-host-ip
Test SSH connection using the new key:
ssh -i ~/.ssh/ansible_key student@target-host-ip
Exit the SSH session:
exit
