Troubleshooting Common Issues
SSH Connection Issues
If you encounter SSH connection problems:

Verify SSH key permissions:
chmod 600 ~/.ssh/ansible_key
chmod 644 ~/.ssh/ansible_key.pub
Test manual SSH connection:
ssh -i ~/.ssh/ansible_key -v student@target-host-ip
Check SSH agent:
ssh-add ~/.ssh/ansible_key
ssh-add -l
Git Authentication Issues
If Git synchronization fails:

Verify token permissions in your Git provider
Test token manually:
git clone https://username:token@github.com/username/repository.git
Check repository URL format in AWX project settings
Privilege Escalation Issues
If sudo operations fail:

Verify sudo configuration on target hosts:
sudo visudo
# Ensure user has appropriate sudo privileges
Test manual privilege escalation:
ansible target-host-ip -i inventory -m shell -a "sudo whoami" --private-key ~/.ssh/ansible_key
